<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muhammad Salahuddin of Bima</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">20th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Muhammad Salahuddin of Bima was the last sultan of Bima, on the island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumbawa">Sumbawa</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, reigning from 1915 to 1951. Bima was then a self-governing domain of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-indies">Dutch East Indies</a>. After the Japanese occupation he supported the Republic of Indonesia and brought his sultanate into it, and its special status ended in 1958.</p></div>
